      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MASTER LOUEY (10) led and saw it through in a 2200m race at Ballarat last start, a deserved win on the back of some solid recent performances. Hard to know where he gets to from this second row draw but races well at this shorter distance. Big chance with even luck. METRO MEMORY (5) overcame a back row draw when he scored last time out by 1.2 metres in a nice return to form at Echuca. Must raise the bar but his strike rate at this circuit and distance stands at 50 per cent and he is better served by this barrier. TOORAM DANNY (9) has to come into calculations on the back of some strong recent form, missing narrowly when second at Echuca last week to give him a win and three placings from the last five starts. SIR NIPPA (3) has won when fresh before and should not have any excuses from the favourable draw.",
